<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Centcelles</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> · Also known as Centcelles Mausoleum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Centcelles is a Roman villa near Constantí, close to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarragona">Tarragona</a> in Catalonia, whose 4th-century domed hall preserves one of the oldest surviving Christian dome mosaics, with hunting and biblical scenes. The hall may have been the mausoleum of the emperor Constans, who was killed in 350. It forms part of the Archaeological Ensemble of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarraco">Tarraco</a> World Heritage Site.</p></div>
